---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, BLOG_TITLE } from '../consts';

const title = `About | ${SITE_TITLE}`;
const description =
	'Brant Gehrke (Sargoto) on information security work, the home lab, streaming, and how one led to the others.';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="prose">
			<div class="about-header">
				<img
					src="/images/avatar-placeholder.svg"
					alt=""
					width="160"
					height="160"
					class="avatar"
				/>
				<div>
					<h1>Who is Sargoto?</h1>
					<p>
						Brant Gehrke. Sargoto is the handle — it's been mine online long
						enough that plenty of people know it and not the name on my badge.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p>
				I work in information security. I stream on Twitch. I run a home lab
				that started as one machine and has never stopped expanding. This
				site is where the overlap goes.
			</p>

			<h2>The work</h2>
			<p>
				I'm an Assistant Director in information security at EY, in an
				operations and engineering role. I've been there since 2022.
			</p>
			<p>
				I got here on a route that doesn't show up in many infosec bios.
				Seven years at Cousins Subs, most of them as a general manager. A year
				on a level 1 help desk at the Medical College of Wisconsin. Then a
				decade at Wells Fargo, where I spent most of my time on an operations
				team — problem process coordinator, incident process coordinator,
				change process expert, business systems analyst, plus enough project
				coordination to know I'd rather be closer to the systems.
			</p>
			<p>
				That path looks scattered on paper. It isn't. Every one of those jobs
				was some version of the same problem: something is going wrong
				repeatedly, nobody agrees on who owns it, and the fix has to survive
				contact with people who have other priorities. Running a restaurant
				during a lunch rush and running a major incident bridge are more alike
				than either group would like to admit.
			</p>
			<p>
				The credentials, for the people who need them: associate's degree in
				computer science from WCTC, GIAC GSEC.
			</p>

			<h2>The code</h2>
			<p>
				C# is my strongest language, though it's been a while since I shipped
				anything I'd point at. My Perl is better than my Python, which says
				something about when I learned what. I'm actively fixing the Python
				part.
			</p>
			<p>
				Most of what I build now lives in the home lab — bare-metal Linux with
				Docker on top, and a steady queue of things I want to understand well
				enough to run myself. Lately that means self-hosting, automation
				pipelines, and poking at LLMs hard enough to find where they break.
			</p>

			<h2>The stream</h2>
			<p>
				I stream on Twitch as Sargoto. Variety, genuinely variety — JRPGs,
				shooters, racing, sports games, whatever has my attention that week.
				No content calendar, no niche, no plan to develop one.
			</p>

			<h2>{BLOG_TITLE}</h2>
			<p>
				The blog. Occasional, opinionated, and usually about something that
				annoyed me enough to write it down. Games, tech, the industry, and the
				places those overlap. If you came here from a rant, that's the
				section you want.
			</p>

			<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Twitch: <a href="https://twitch.tv/sargoto" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">twitch.tv/sargoto</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					LinkedIn: <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/brantgehrke" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">linkedin.com/in/brantgehrke</a>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="disclaimer">
				Opinions here are mine and not my employer's, which should go without
				saying but apparently never does.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	.about-header {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.5em;
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
	}
	.avatar {
		border-radius: 50%;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.about-header h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0.25em;
	}
	.disclaimer {
		margin-top: 2em;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		font-style: italic;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	@media (max-width: 500px) {
		.about-header {
			flex-direction: column;
			align-items: flex-start;
		}
	}
</style>
